 be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.8 to 6.8. December accounts for 16% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 17% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 76 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution is expected in other months. The number of different contractors does not prove any single contract was improperly awarded.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistency with other months. Verify if the same contractor was used for multiple similar needs. Review the contract details to ensure no repeated orders for the same service.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["J0dl7dr8zSucCF8sV%2BqtYA%3D%3D","Ud8Rpygrn%2FXIGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","FTA4mySk5v570UvEyYJSGw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}